{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Its tongs.</b> A kind of pincers with which one draws the wick to whichever side he wishes." "<b>Its pans.</b> Like a small shovel, its edges flat and not rounded, and it has no partition in front but only at its sides, and with it one scoops the ash of the lamps when he tends them." "<b>Its lamps.</b> לוצי״ש בְּלַעַז — into which one puts the oil and the wicks."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French loise, 'lamps'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:20.446719854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}